{"mt_tconst": "lincoln", "mt_cr": ["Total Film", "Kate Stables"], "mt_cr_review_score": 80, "mt_cr_review_date": "Jan 11, 2013", "mt_cr_review": "Steeped in the bitter political divisions of the Civil War, Spielberg's thrilling film about hardwon freedoms is immersed in its own time, but speaks eloquently to ours.", "mt_cr_review_full_url": "http://www.totalfilm.com/reviews/cinema/lincoln", "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/movie/lincoln/critic-reviews", "spider": "mt_cr_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"mt_tconst": "lincoln", "mt_cr": ["Slate", "Dana Stevens"], "mt_cr_review_score": 80, "mt_cr_review_date": "Jan  1, 2013", "mt_cr_review": "Lincoln does sometimes get a little sappy around the edges. Though his project here is clearly one of conscious self-restraint, Spielberg can't resist the occasional opportunity for patriotic tear-jerking, usually signaled by a swell of John Williams' symphonic score. But in between, there are long stretches that are as quiet, contemplative, and austere as anything Spielberg has ever done.", "mt_cr_review_full_url": "http://www.slate.com/articles/arts/movies/2012/11/lincoln_directed_by_steven_spielberg_starring_daniel_day_lewis_reviewed.html", "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/movie/lincoln/critic-reviews", "spider": "mt_cr_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
{"mt_tconst": "lincoln", "mt_cr": ["NPR", "Ian Buckwalter"], "mt_cr_review_score": 80, "mt_cr_review_date": "Nov  8, 2012", "mt_cr_review": "This Lincoln isn't an abstracted, infallible ideal, but rather a deeply conflicted, often lonely leader simply trying to do the right thing - even if that means few wrong things along on the way.", "mt_cr_review_full_url": "http://www.npr.org/2012/11/08/162794255/lincoln-a-great-emancipator-but-not-quite-a-saint", "url": "https://www.metacritic.com/movie/lincoln/critic-reviews", "spider": "mt_cr_review", "date": "20/08/2021"}
